    <item>
      <title>Young people are having less sex. What's going on? - video</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/science/video/2026/nov/26/young-people-are-having-less-sex-than-ever-whats-going-on-video</link>
      <description>Sex among British adults has slumped in recent decades, with under-45s having half as many monthly encounters as in 1990 and one in three under-25s reporting that they have never had sexual intercourse. To unpick some of the possible reasons behind these declines, Madeleine Finlay hears from science editor and co-host Ian Sample. He tells her why young people might be having sex later, and what could account for the striking rise in women reporting that they don’t want children. Continue…</description>
