      <title>How a new way of measuring tides could make flood forecasts more accurate</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/science/2026/nov/25/new-way-of-measuring-tides-flood-forecasts-accurate</link>
      <description>Analysis of differences in tidal height across beaches could lead to more localised tide and flood forecasts The sea might look level, but it turns out tidal height can vary by as much as a metre across the length of a single beach, new research shows. This development is important when it comes to flood predictions and when forecasting which locations are most vulnerable to storm surges. Up until now, our knowledge of tidal levels has been limited. Tide gauges tell us about a specific…</description>
